{"name":"Jazz Age Coral","hex":"#f1bfb1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jazz","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical art form rooted in West African cultural and musical expression and in the African American blues tradition, with diverse influences over time, commonly characterized by blue notes, syncopation, swing, call and response, polyrhythms and improvisation.","Energy, excitement, excitability."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To destroy; to ruin.","To play (jazz music)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jazz"},{"term":"age","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Angal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The amount of time that some being has been alive, or that some thing has been in existence, as measured from its birth or origin until the present or until some other given reference point. (Often measured in number of years;  alternatively in months, days, hours, etc.; see also the usage notes)","The state of being old; the latter part of life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/age"},{"term":"coral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many species of marine invertebrates in the class Anthozoa, most of which build hard calcium carbonate skeletons and form colonies, or a colony belonging to one of those species.","A hard substance made of the skeletons of these organisms."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of coral.","Having the orange-pink color of coral."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jazz Age","blocks":[{"text":"The Jazz Age was a period from 1920 to the early 1930s in which jazz music and dance styles gained worldwide popularity. The Jazz Age's cultural repercussions were primarily felt in the United States, the birthplace of jazz. Originating in New Orleans as mainly sourced from the culture of African Americans, jazz played a significant part in wider cultural changes in this period, and its influence on popular culture continued long afterwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/CarterAndKingJazzingOrchestra.jpg/330px-CarterAndKingJazzingOrchestra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz_Age","wikidata":"Q388483"},{"title":"Jazz","blocks":[{"text":"Jazz is a music genre that originated in the African-American communities of New Orleans, Louisiana, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Its roots are in blues, ragtime, European harmony, African rhythmic rituals, spirituals, hymns, marches, vaudeville song, and dance music. Since the 1920s Jazz Age, it has been recognized as a major form of musical expression in both traditional and popular music. Jazz is characterized by swing and blue notes, complex chords, call and response vocals, polyrhythms and improvisation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz","wikidata":"Q8341"},{"title":"Coral","blocks":[{"text":"Corals are colonial marine invertebrates within the subphylum Anthozoa of the phylum Cnidaria. They typically form compact colonies of many identical individual polyps. Coral species include the important reef builders that inhabit tropical oceans and secrete calcium carbonate to form a hard skeleton."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg/330px-Coral_Outcrop_Flynn_Reef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral","wikidata":"Q171446"},{"title":"Coral (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The various tones of the color coral are orange, red and pink representations of the colors of those cnidarians known as precious corals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coral_(color)","wikidata":"Q2411228"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/JohnHeld_Tales_of_the_Jazz_Age_1922.jpg/330px-JohnHeld_Tales_of_the_Jazz_Age_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/JohnHeld_Tales_of_the_Jazz_Age_1922.jpg/330px-JohnHeld_Tales_of_the_Jazz_Age_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohnHeld_Tales_of_the_Jazz_Age_1922.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/500px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/1280px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg/500px-Bessie_Smith_%281936%29_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABessie_Smith_(1936)_by_Carl_Van_Vechten.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Fate_Marable%27s_New_Orleans_Band_on_the_S._S._Sidney.jpg/500px-Fate_Marable%27s_New_Orleans_Band_on_the_S._S._Sidney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Fate_Marable%27s_New_Orleans_Band_on_the_S._S._Sidney.jpg/500px-Fate_Marable%27s_New_Orleans_Band_on_the_S._S._Sidney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFate_Marable's_New_Orleans_Band_on_the_S._S._Sidney.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Frank_Farnum_coaching_Pauline_Starke.jpg/500px-Frank_Farnum_coachi